the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base uses temporal includes these resources:
    temporal.

the templates are:
    *a person* was born on *a date*; undefined.
    *a person* can drive on *a date*.
    *a person* claimed *an amount* on *a date*; undefined.
    the recent claims of *a person* on *a date* total *an amount*.

the knowledge base uses temporal includes:

a person can drive on a date if
    the person was born on a birth date
    and the age on the date of someone born on the birth date is a number N
    and N >= 16.

the recent claims of a person on a date total an amount T if
    the person was born on a birth date
    and T is the sum of each A such that
        the person claimed an amount A on a claim date
        and the claim date is within the last 3 months before the date.

scenario one is:
    ann was born on 2008-03-15.
    bob was born on 2010-01-01.
    ann claimed 100 on 2026-08-01.
    ann claimed 50 on 2026-05-01.
    drive expects answers ["ann can drive on 2026-09-13", "bob can drive on 2026-09-13"].
    claims expects answers ["the recent claims of ann on 2026-09-13 total 100", "the recent claims of bob on 2026-09-13 total 0"].

query drive is:
    which person can drive on 2026-09-13.

query claims is:
    the recent claims of which person on 2026-09-13 total which amount.
